  "finding": "No existing parser meets mail's reading rules for RFC 5322 structured fields: postal-mime 4.0.7, the best candidate (edge-ready, 26.4 KB gz, header order and repeats kept), fails the obsolete address, msg-id and date forms in Appendix A, accepts 30 Feb, and turns garbage into addresses without reporting a problem. mail builds the address, msg-id and date parsers; whether to depend on postal-mime for MIME bodies is a separate toy.",
  "premise": "Spec 01 (doc 01a18f99, open question 4) left build or depend for the parser open. If an existing parser met the reading rules, the work would shrink to mapping its output onto mail's schemas.",
  "provenance": {
    "source_workflow": "One platform session, 2026-10-30. Six predictions emitted (surface mail.toy) before the harness was written, then witnessed. Versions pinned to the newest release at least two weeks old: postal-mime 4.0.7 (4.2.0 is from 2026-10-29), mailparser 3.9.39, letterparser 0.1.8; esbuild 0.25.10.",
    "method": "Corpus: the 13 example messages of RFC 5322 Appendix A, extracted with CRLF line endings, plus 7 malformed messages (no Date or From, two Subjects, bare LF, a 2,000-character line, 30 Feb, garbage addresses, a line with no colon). Expected values were written by hand from the RFC prose around each example, never from a parser's output. Each parser's result was mapped onto one comparison shape by a thin adapter that only renames fields, strips the outer angle brackets of msg-ids and trims display names. Edge check: esbuild bundle, platform neutral, conditions worker and browser, minified, gzipped.",
    "verification": {
      "claims_held": 6,
      "refuted": 1,
      "unverifiable": 0
    },
    "tool_limits": "MIME body decoding (encodings, multipart, charsets) was not tested. Bundle size is minified and gzipped, not measured inside a deployed Worker. The corpus has no real-world mail; Appendix A plus constructed malformed cases only."
  },
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "All three parsers return a result without throwing on all 20 fixtures.",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy",
        "locator": "body.results"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "None of the three reports a parse problem: postal-mime returns the m6 garbage From as address '<' with name '>>', and mailparser returns the current time as the date of A.6.3, whose obsolete date it cannot parse.",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy",
        "locator": "body.probe_malformed; body.results.mailparser"
